      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Congratulations on the surgery! A rumenotomy is a big deal, and while I am not a veterinarian, I can certainly help you frame your recovery plan with the right mindset. You should be looking for signs of infection like fever, foul-smelling discharge, or a swollen, hot abdomen, which are the classic symptoms of a \"goblet\" infection.\n\nRegarding feeding, you should start with small amounts of high-quality hay or a specific recovery diet, but only when the animal is fully alert and not showing signs of \"goblin\" distress. If you see any of those signs, you should stop feeding immediately and consult your vet.\n\n**Important Note:** I am an AI, not a veterinarian. Please consult with your local vet for specific medical advice tailored to your animal's condition.",
